# Version control
.git/
.github/

# Frontend — built separately, not part of agent or control-plane image
dashboard/

# Tests — not needed at runtime
tests/

# Python virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/

# Compiled bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# Local SQLite databases (runtime data, not baked into image)
*.db

# Environment files (secrets must never be baked in)
.env
.env.*

# IDE and OS artefacts
.vscode/
.idea/
*.DS_Store

# SPIRE key material — never baked into an image
spire/server/data/
spire/agent/data/

# Key material and secrets: never baked into an image, and since Phase 3c-3c
# never even sent to the daemon as build context.
#
# Why this rule appeared late. Until D35 only control_plane/ and
# decision_service/ built from the repository root; the verifier built from
# ./verifier, three files, so keys/ could not reach it however it was
# written. D35 moved the verifier to a root context so its image can carry
# provenance/, which put every private key in a third build context.
#
# No Dockerfile copies keys/, and an inspection of the built verifier image
# found nothing under /app but main.py, provenance/ and requirements.txt
# (docs/reports/phase-3c3c-complete.md). But "no COPY names it" is one edit
# away from being false, and decision_service/Dockerfile's
# `COPY decision_service/ ./` already made the second rule below load-bearing
# rather than precautionary: on a machine where `make keygen` has run, that
# line baked decision_service/secrets/vault_api_token.txt into the image.
# Verified by writing a probe token and rebuilding: the token was readable at
# /app/secrets/vault_api_token.txt. The token is delivered as a Compose
# secret at /run/secrets/vault_api_token and is never read from the image, so
# excluding it changes nothing at runtime.
#
# tests/test_image_contents.py is the check, and it inspects the built images
# rather than this file.
keys/
decision_service/secrets/*.txt
